set_new('E-48', '''3. You: delete BOTH HubSpot private apps (Settings, Integrations, Private Apps, Delete) by Mon 23 Nov 2026 18:29 UTC = 23:59 IST (the end of the spending window, the same as the rest of this step). Make a screenshot (a picture of your screen). Before you save it, crop it (cut away the parts of the picture) so that it shows no secret key text, no account name and no web address.
   Item 3 has a second job with an EARLIER deadline: the secret key for the model (the long text that lets the model stage use the AI model and spend money). Parts 3a to 3j are for that key only.
   3a. The fixed rule. The secret key for the model that the take used ends by Mon 23 Nov 2026 18:19 UTC = 23:49 IST at the latest (the last time to revoke), WHATEVER you answer to any question below, and `not sure` never keeps it alive. To revoke is to delete a key at the company that issued it, so that it stops working. This is the security decision of 16 Nov 2026 (the owner revokes the key), confirmed in writing by the studio lead. Your answers only decide whether you first make new keys for your own n8n and for other things that use the same key (part 3g). The spending window ends 10 minutes later, at 18:29 UTC = 23:59 IST; that is when the model stage must stop spending.
   3b. Your alarm. The assistant has no timer, and nobody else reminds you on Mon 23 Nov 2026. Set an alarm on your own phone or computer for Mon 23 Nov 2026 17:49 UTC = 23:19 IST and name it `revoke the model key`. When it rings, do part 3h at once if you have not done it yet; if you have, the alarm costs you nothing. If a session with the assistant is open at that time it asks "Is the key revoked?" first, but do not count on it.
   3c. Two routes. The assistant recommends route B; the choice is yours. After EVERY take the assistant asks you to reply `no more takes` or `more takes`; no reply counts as `more takes`. If it forgets to ask, you may write `no more takes` at any time. Route A: you write `no more takes` right after the last take that you want, and then do parts 3d to 3h at once, normally on Wed 18 Nov 2026. Cost of A: if the cut (step 21) then turns out bad, no further take is possible with that key; you would first make a new secret key and give a new yes (step 20). Route B (recommended): you write `no more takes` only after you have written `cut accepted` (step 21). Benefit of B: a retake is possible after a bad cut. Cost of B: the key and its copy in the take folder stay alive for up to five days (Wed 18 Nov to Mon 23 Nov 2026), and the revoke on the last day depends on you and your alarm (part 3b). In route B you must watch the cut and write `cut accepted` and `no more takes` before Mon 23 Nov 2026 18:19 UTC = 23:49 IST; if you have not by then, you revoke at that time anyway (part 3j).
   3d. What the assistant does at once. In its next message after your `no more takes`, the assistant gives you (1) the full path of the take folder and the full path of the copy of the key inside it, (2) the two questions of part 3e, and (3) the steps of parts 3f to 3h with the exact page of the key list. If it does not, ask it.
   3e. Two questions. Question 1: "Is the secret key for the model that you saved one that you made only for this take, and does nothing else use it?" Reply `yes`, `no, other things use it` or `not sure`. Question 2: "Is the saved key the same one that is stored in your own n8n, the one that you open at `http://localhost:5678`? If it is, revoking it breaks that n8n." Reply `same key`, `different key` or `not sure`. (The port number is the number after the colon in a web address.) The assistant also asked both before the take (see the note at the top of Phase 0); it asks again because your answers may have changed. Any other reply counts as `not sure`. Only `yes` together with `different key` means that nothing has to be replaced first; every other pair means part 3g comes before part 3h.
   3f. Shred the copy in the take folder now. The model stage reads a copy of the secret key that you placed in the take folder. Delete that copy with `shred -u <path>`, where `<path>` is the full path that the assistant gave you in part 3d. Before you run it, check three things: the path starts with the full path of the take folder (it must lie inside the take folder); it contains no `..`; and `ls -l <path>` shows a line that starts with `-` (a plain file, not a link). If any of the three is not so, do not run the command and tell the assistant. The assistant never opens the file. To shred is to overwrite the content of a file before it is removed, so that the old content is harder to recover; a plain delete (`rm`) only removes the file's name. If shred is not installed, use `rm <path>`. Shredding does not revoke the key, and it is not reliable on every disk (flash disks and disks that keep a journal may keep the old content), so it does not replace part 3h. Item 1 later removes the take folder with a plain delete, which is neither a shred nor a revoke.
   3g. Make new keys first, if you need to. If your answers were anything but `yes` together with `different key`, other things may use the key. (1) If it is the key of your own n8n: make a new secret key on the same website as in part 3h, apply the typing rule (step 8, sub-step a: write `please stop looking`, wait for `not looking`, type or paste the new key into the credential in your own n8n by hand, copy any made-up word to clear the clipboard, write `you may look again`), replace the old key in that credential and test your n8n once. (2) If other things use the key, tell the assistant what they are (names only, never the key) and make a new key for each of them in the same way. If fewer than 20 minutes remain before 18:19 UTC = 23:49 IST, skip to part 3h: the key still ends and the other things stop working. If you cannot name the other things that use it, the key still ends and they stop working; the assistant lists them in the handoff.
   3h. Revoke the key, ALWAYS, by 18:19 UTC = 23:49 IST on Mon 23 Nov 2026 at the latest. Revoke it on the website of the company that provides the AI model (Anthropic). The assistant tells you the exact page before the clean-up; that click path is not checked. Find the key in the list by its NAME and by the LAST FOUR CHARACTERS that the list shows for it, and compare them with your own saved note of the key. You compare them yourself: never tell the assistant the characters of a key. If you are not sure which key it is, do not revoke any other key: tell the assistant what the list shows (names and dates only) and wait for its answer, but keep the deadline. Open the key list again after a few minutes. When the key is gone from the list, write `key revoked`. If you could not revoke it by the deadline, write `key not revoked` and the reason; the assistant lists it in the handoff with a date to finish it. Make a screenshot of the list as your own record: crop it so that it shows the key names and dates but no account name, no web address and no key characters. The screenshot is a record only; it does not prove that the right key is gone, because the assistant cannot tell from a picture which key is which.
   3i. Other secret keys for the model: every key except the one that the take ran on (that one is part 3h). Revoke another key only if all three are so: you know what it is for and nothing uses it; the list says it was last used more than 7 days ago; and it is not a key that an n8n holds (your own n8n or the take's n8n), because such a key may look unused. If any of the three is not so, leave the key alone and tell the assistant which key it is; the assistant lists it in the handoff.
   3j. If a take is still running at 18:19 UTC = 23:49 IST on Mon 23 Nov 2026 (a take runs that day only under the condition stated in the request for your yes, step 16): tell the assistant at once and revoke the key at that time anyway (part 3h), unless the assistant tells you otherwise before that time. A revoked key cannot spend money, and the take then fails. The assistant then tells you in writing what happens next: which part of the take is finished, which part is not, and what you have to clean up by hand. That the take stops safely when its key is revoked is not proven (UNVERIFIED).
   The assistant never opens the key file (this is a procedure, not enforced by a program). No check in item 5 tests the secret key for the model.
   Your own copies of the secret key are the files where you saved it; tell the assistant only the path, never the content. When the key is revoked, shred every file that holds a copy of the OLD key with `shred -u <file>` (if shred is not installed, use `rm <file>`), as in item 6. Files that hold a NEW key made in part 3g stay, because that key is in use. The two secret files in `~/take-secrets` (the file with the app password of the mailbox that receives the take's mails, called the receiver mailbox, and the file with the HubSpot read secret key) are covered by item 6. Until the key is revoked, keep its copies.''')
